{
  "_comment": [
    "Example MCP wiring for the optional knowledge runtime.",
    "Copy to .mcp.json (already gitignored) and replace both /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/VAULT",
    "placeholders with this vault's real path.",
    "",
    "USE ABSOLUTE PATHS. A client may start a stdio server from any working",
    "directory, so a relative 'command' or 'args' entry resolves against a",
    "directory you do not control and the server never starts. .mcp.json is",
    "gitignored precisely so it can hold machine-specific absolute paths.",
    "",
    "'command' must be the interpreter that has agentic_vault_knowledge installed:",
    "  <vault>/.venv/bin/python        (macOS/Linux)",
    "  <vault>/.venv/Scripts/python.exe (Windows)",
    "A bare 'python' only works if the runtime is on the default interpreter.",
    "",
    "The launcher then resolves the vault root from its own __file__ location, so",
    "you do not need to set AGENTIC_VAULT_ROOT and the server works regardless of",
    "the working directory it was started in. That is the launcher's job; locating",
    "the launcher itself is this file's job, which is why the paths are absolute.",
    "",
    "Writes are OFF by default. To allow knowledge_apply_patch/apply_batch to",
    "mutate canonical Markdown, add:",
    "  \"env\": { \"AGENTIC_VAULT_KNOWLEDGE_READ_ONLY\": \"0\" }",
    "",
    "Claude Code users may substitute ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.} for the vault path,",
    "but only if the server is always started with the vault as the project root:",
    "CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is set in the SERVER's environment, not the client's, so it",
    "is empty at config-expansion time and the :-. default leaves a cwd-relative",
    "path. Absolute paths avoid that failure mode entirely."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "vault-knowledge": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/VAULT/.venv/bin/python",
      "args": [
        "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/VAULT/.agent/scripts/vault-knowledge-mcp.py"
      ]
    }
  }
}
